WEBVTT

00:00:02.300 --> 00:00:05.040
I wonder what it will be?

00:00:05.270 --> 00:00:07.610
This week, it's this!

00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:10.860
Another black card?

00:00:10.860 --> 00:00:12.930
What kind of monster is it?

00:00:12.930 --> 00:00:14.740
For details, watch the show!

00:00:23.320 --> 00:00:25.560
I also need to speak with Godwin.

00:00:29.620 --> 00:00:32.840
What?  You piece of Satellite garbage!

00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:37.230
Take me there.

00:00:39.510 --> 00:00:44.060
You won't be acting tough 
for much longer, punk!

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:46.980
I'll deal with you personally!

00:00:48.260 --> 00:00:49.480
Hurry up.

00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:07.700
Looking over a vast distance

00:01:07.960 --> 00:01:12.800
I realized my field of vision was narrow

00:01:13.070 --> 00:01:17.710
Even if it’s easier to throw myself away

00:01:18.070 --> 00:01:22.480
I want to survive to the best of my abilities

00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:27.850
No matter how bad today is

00:01:29.420 --> 00:01:32.830
There’s still the faintest light

00:01:34.590 --> 00:01:38.230
All I have to do tomorrow

00:01:38.530 --> 00:01:42.300
Is light it myself

00:01:42.600 --> 00:01:47.300
I test myself so I won’t stop or vanish

00:01:47.670 --> 00:01:52.270
Even if I get countless scars

00:01:52.770 --> 00:01:58.570
I ride wishing for the 
arrival of a true tomorrow

00:01:58.880 --> 00:02:02.550
Today will never exist again

00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:08.450
So I won’t stop or vanish

00:02:32.210 --> 00:02:38.270
Threat Approaching!
Dark Signer Ushio!?

00:02:40.280 --> 00:02:41.350
Here you go.

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:45.310
It's missing.

00:02:45.310 --> 00:02:48.520
It's missing!

00:02:48.520 --> 00:02:50.760
You must be kidding me!

00:02:50.760 --> 00:02:55.120
Where's my camera?  Where's my scoop?  
You were holding on to it for me!

00:02:55.120 --> 00:02:56.360
Camera?

00:02:57.400 --> 00:02:59.450
There's no record of it.

00:02:59.450 --> 00:03:03.650
That's not true!  I 
definitely gave it to you!

00:03:04.150 --> 00:03:04.920
Hello?

00:03:04.920 --> 00:03:09.120
Carly, what are you doing?  I 
kept the front page open for you!

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:11.840
And Angela of the Daily Duel 
got the scoop instead of you!

00:03:11.840 --> 00:03:13.460
I'm sorry.

00:03:13.460 --> 00:03:15.420
If you don't bring me 
anything good, you're fired!

00:03:15.420 --> 00:03:18.140
Editor!

00:03:27.520 --> 00:03:30.070
This is the worst!

00:03:30.070 --> 00:03:32.490
But I'm not going to give up.

00:03:33.020 --> 00:03:35.650
I'll draw today's fortune.

00:03:36.350 --> 00:03:37.540
Draw!

00:03:37.890 --> 00:03:40.760
This is Fortune Fairy Swee.

00:03:41.180 --> 00:03:47.060
By drawing this card, today's 
fortune is... slightly bad.

00:03:47.060 --> 00:03:48.950
I feel like giving up.

00:03:48.950 --> 00:03:51.920
No!  I won't give up!  On to my next report!

00:03:52.220 --> 00:03:58.220
That's right!  Today is the sneak preview 
of the movie "Lord of the King!"

00:03:59.950 --> 00:04:01.760
How ironic.

00:04:01.760 --> 00:04:05.320
They're using this sneak preview 
to promote the documentary film

00:04:05.320 --> 00:04:10.320
about the King.  However, it turns out 
the King is just an ordinary person.

00:04:10.320 --> 00:04:12.950
The celebrities on the red carpet 
aren't that special either.

00:04:12.950 --> 00:04:16.410
They should change the title 
to "Lord of the Former King."

00:04:16.410 --> 00:04:19.070
Excuse me.  Let me through.

00:04:19.070 --> 00:04:20.870
What's with you?

00:04:23.770 --> 00:04:24.700
Hey!

00:04:24.700 --> 00:04:25.920
Stop pushing!

00:04:26.430 --> 00:04:27.630
Angela.

00:04:27.630 --> 00:04:29.620
Oh, it's you.

00:04:29.620 --> 00:04:33.130
You're covering a party in that ugly costume?

00:04:33.450 --> 00:04:35.490
How scary.

00:04:35.490 --> 00:04:40.600
Today is a once-in-a-lifetime event.  
Shouldn't you wear proper attire?

00:04:40.600 --> 00:04:42.170
Wow!

00:04:43.200 --> 00:04:45.810
That's the world's top model!

00:04:46.610 --> 00:04:48.090
It's Misty!

00:04:48.440 --> 00:04:50.590
She's beautiful!

00:04:57.960 --> 00:04:59.790
I'm just imagining things.

00:05:13.610 --> 00:05:14.490
Director!

00:05:14.490 --> 00:05:15.630
Director!

00:05:15.980 --> 00:05:19.970
Everyone, we've created a fabulous movie.

00:05:19.970 --> 00:05:23.880
What is the King?  What should the King be?

00:05:23.880 --> 00:05:28.530
All the answers are in this movie!

00:05:34.700 --> 00:05:35.860
Duel!

00:05:40.280 --> 00:05:41.630
There's only one King!

00:05:42.090 --> 00:05:43.280
It's me!

00:05:43.410 --> 00:05:46.760
A King's duel must be entertaining!

00:05:48.010 --> 00:05:52.930
Jack Atlas was born in the 
Tops area of Neo Domino City.

00:05:52.930 --> 00:05:57.800
Please continue to enjoy "Lord of the King."

00:05:58.590 --> 00:06:00.220
If you'll excuse me.

00:06:00.220 --> 00:06:01.540
Wait a second!

00:06:03.430 --> 00:06:08.380
This narration is incorrect!  It 
says Jack was born in the Tops.

00:06:10.290 --> 00:06:16.700
You know that Jack was born in 
Satellite, just like Yusei Fudo.

00:06:20.550 --> 00:06:22.280
What do you mean?

00:06:22.280 --> 00:06:26.640
If that's true, since you're in charge 
of Security, it means you gave

00:06:26.640 --> 00:06:31.640
special treatment to a Satellite citizen 
so that he could live in Neo Domino City!

00:06:31.640 --> 00:06:35.310
It means the Director broke the law!

00:06:35.840 --> 00:06:39.770
I won't respond to such 
unreliable speculation.

00:06:40.040 --> 00:06:42.240
Now I must take my leave.

00:06:44.020 --> 00:06:46.950
Wait, Director Godwin!

00:06:46.950 --> 00:06:47.800
Director!

00:06:49.790 --> 00:06:52.270
Is what she said about the King true?

00:06:52.270 --> 00:06:54.420
Sorry to keep you waiting.  I'm the King!

00:06:55.400 --> 00:06:56.920
I'm going to investigate.

00:06:58.990 --> 00:07:00.210
Hey you.

00:07:02.950 --> 00:07:05.530
M-M-Misty!

00:07:06.330 --> 00:07:09.970
Your face really interests me.

00:07:10.530 --> 00:07:11.750
And…

00:07:12.520 --> 00:07:15.370
I apologize for my face.

00:07:15.790 --> 00:07:18.020
I like fortunetelling.

00:07:18.020 --> 00:07:22.140
Me too.  I do card fortune-telling.

00:07:22.140 --> 00:07:25.390
I look at faces.

00:07:28.370 --> 00:07:30.730
I see death.

00:07:31.820 --> 00:07:33.870
You're going to die soon.

00:07:35.810 --> 00:07:36.820
I see.

00:07:37.030 --> 00:07:42.800
But when that time comes, we'll be 
able to understand each other better.

00:07:44.610 --> 00:07:45.700
Excuse me!

00:07:45.700 --> 00:07:49.900
Thank you very much, but 
I'm in a hurry.  Sorry!

00:07:53.410 --> 00:07:55.670
What's with her?

00:07:59.140 --> 00:08:00.800
When is Godwin coming?

00:08:00.800 --> 00:08:04.780
Be patient.  The Director is a busy man.

00:08:04.780 --> 00:08:09.520
If you're so bored, then why don't I 
duel you until the Director arrives?

00:08:09.520 --> 00:08:14.120
If I defeat this Satellite 
garbage, then I'll be the King.

00:08:15.420 --> 00:08:16.960
That would be bad.

00:08:17.360 --> 00:08:22.040
Even though the new King won't 
lose to someone like you.

00:08:22.040 --> 00:08:23.310
What?

00:08:23.710 --> 00:08:28.520
Sorry to keep you waiting.  The 
Director has asked for you.

00:08:29.690 --> 00:08:32.990
Pick up Jack from the hospital.

00:08:33.390 --> 00:08:36.130
He also wants to talk with Jack.

00:08:37.800 --> 00:08:40.170
Understood.

00:08:48.440 --> 00:08:52.600
After losing to the Satellite 
duelist last night, Jack

00:08:52.600 --> 00:08:56.600
Atlas was taken to this hospital.  
Many reporters are here to-

00:08:56.950 --> 00:08:58.070
Sorry!

00:08:58.070 --> 00:08:59.890
What's with that kid!

00:09:00.830 --> 00:09:04.440
I'm sorry!  Last night, 
the Satellite duelist...

00:09:05.460 --> 00:09:07.310
It worked.

00:09:10.040 --> 00:09:11.380
You must be kidding me!

00:09:12.850 --> 00:09:15.200
Treating me like a servant!

00:09:28.160 --> 00:09:29.860
Stop!

00:09:51.650 --> 00:09:53.930
Leave me alone.

00:10:13.240 --> 00:10:15.090
Jack's hospital room is…

00:10:16.970 --> 00:10:18.410
Jack!

00:10:27.930 --> 00:10:30.410
If I remember correctly,  he's from Security.

00:10:38.810 --> 00:10:41.920
What's going on?  Why do you have that mark?

00:10:44.050 --> 00:10:45.720
Attack Sonic Chick!

00:10:45.720 --> 00:10:47.440
Blizzard Strike!

00:10:52.230 --> 00:10:53.690
He has the same glow on his arm!

00:10:56.350 --> 00:10:58.330
You're also a Signer?

00:10:58.730 --> 00:11:02.020
I'm a Dark Signer.

00:11:02.480 --> 00:11:07.560
After five thousand years, I've 
come for you from the underworld.

00:11:08.050 --> 00:11:10.280
I will take the light.

00:11:10.420 --> 00:11:12.250
Dark Signer?

00:11:12.570 --> 00:11:18.710
You can't duel him, Jack!  Yusei battled 
against a duelist who had the same mark.

00:11:18.710 --> 00:11:21.790
What, Yusei?  How did he do?

00:11:21.790 --> 00:11:23.180
He won.

00:11:24.960 --> 00:11:25.700
You!

00:11:25.700 --> 00:11:26.900
Yes?

00:11:26.900 --> 00:11:29.820
I don't know who you are, 
but do you know how to duel?

00:11:29.820 --> 00:11:31.790
I can, but…

00:11:31.790 --> 00:11:32.880
In that case...

00:11:33.840 --> 00:11:35.110
You'll be my hands.

00:11:35.750 --> 00:11:38.330
Hold the cards for me and draw!

00:11:39.440 --> 00:11:40.380
But…

00:11:40.710 --> 00:11:43.300
If Yusei won, then this won't be a problem.

00:11:43.300 --> 00:11:47.070
I'll annihilate him in this duel 
and ask him why he's doing this!

00:11:47.980 --> 00:11:50.260
Let's start.  Put on the Duel Disk!

00:11:50.260 --> 00:11:51.330
Okay.

00:11:53.220 --> 00:11:54.170
Here I go!

00:11:54.380 --> 00:11:55.390
Duel!

00:11:55.530 --> 00:11:57.150
I said that out loud!

00:12:04.540 --> 00:12:05.980
You're glowing too!

00:12:06.160 --> 00:12:07.620
What's this?

00:12:07.620 --> 00:12:13.210
The same thing happened during the duel 
between Yusei Fudo and the man with the spider mark.

00:12:13.210 --> 00:12:15.280
It's my turn.

00:12:17.330 --> 00:12:20.440
I summon Warm Worm in defense position!

00:12:24.450 --> 00:12:26.870
I know I can succeed!

00:12:26.870 --> 00:12:30.880
There's no bigger scoop than 
dueling alongside Jack!

00:12:31.120 --> 00:12:32.130
It's my tur-

00:12:32.130 --> 00:12:33.250
It's my turn!

00:12:33.250 --> 00:12:34.370
I apologize.

00:12:34.470 --> 00:12:37.810
From my hand, I Special Summon Vice Dragon!

00:12:37.820 --> 00:12:38.700
Right.

00:12:41.670 --> 00:12:45.520
When you have a monster on your 
field but none on my field, I can

00:12:45.520 --> 00:12:52.520
Special Summon it from my hand by 
halving its attack and defense points.

00:12:52.890 --> 00:12:58.770
Then I release Vice Dragon to 
Advance Summon Strong Wind Dragon!

00:13:01.510 --> 00:13:04.990
Then Strong Wind Dragon's 
monster effect activates!

00:13:05.520 --> 00:13:10.170
It gains half the attack points of 
one released Dragon-Type monster!

00:13:11.930 --> 00:13:15.700
Since Vice Dragon has 2000 attack points…

00:13:15.700 --> 00:13:17.140
It gains 1000 points!

00:13:17.880 --> 00:13:19.770
3400?

00:13:20.120 --> 00:13:23.600
Strong Wind Dragon attacks Warm Worm!

00:13:23.860 --> 00:13:25.830
Strong Hurricane!

00:13:28.840 --> 00:13:29.930
What's happening?

00:13:30.220 --> 00:13:33.010
Like I said, this isn't a normal duel!

00:13:33.010 --> 00:13:37.160
I don't really understand, but it seems 
to be a real life-and-death duel.

00:13:37.160 --> 00:13:39.120
That was an actual explosion.

00:13:40.190 --> 00:13:45.100
Why did he lose life points when 
Warm Worm was in defense position?

00:13:45.560 --> 00:13:50.420
Strong Wind Dragon's attack 
deals piercing damage.

00:13:51.350 --> 00:13:52.710
If its attack points are greater 
than the opponent monster's

00:13:52.710 --> 00:13:55.710
defense points, then the opponent loses 
life points equal to the difference.

00:13:55.710 --> 00:13:58.980
Incredible!  No wonder this 
is the former King's deck!

00:13:58.980 --> 00:14:00.440
Former King?

00:14:01.110 --> 00:14:02.520
I mean, umm…

00:14:04.300 --> 00:14:09.880
When Warm Worm is destroyed in battle, you 
send three cards in your deck to your graveyard.

00:14:10.680 --> 00:14:13.440
So I have to send three cards.

00:14:14.190 --> 00:14:15.990
His plan is…

00:14:19.450 --> 00:14:22.640
I set one card and end my turn.

00:14:22.640 --> 00:14:23.460
Right.

00:14:25.880 --> 00:14:27.820
My turn.

00:14:27.820 --> 00:14:31.170
From my hand, I summon Shield 
Worm in defense position!

00:14:31.600 --> 00:14:37.180
When this monster is successfully summoned,  
you send one card in your deck to the graveyard.

00:14:38.140 --> 00:14:39.390
Again?

00:14:44.600 --> 00:14:47.600
I place one card facedown and end my turn.

00:14:47.600 --> 00:14:49.440
My tur…  I mean…

00:14:49.440 --> 00:14:50.920
It's my turn!

00:14:52.920 --> 00:14:58.820
In order to activate this spell card, 
I have to release Strong Wind Dragon.

00:14:58.820 --> 00:15:00.200
Then it's obvious what you're going to do!

00:15:00.200 --> 00:15:03.680
Strong Wind Dragon attacks Shield Worm!

00:15:03.680 --> 00:15:04.430
You idiot!

00:15:04.910 --> 00:15:05.940
I was wrong?

00:15:09.770 --> 00:15:15.010
Due to Shield Worm's monster effect, 
battle damage from your attack becomes 0.

00:15:16.660 --> 00:15:19.980
Strong Wind Dragon's 
piercing damage is negated!

00:15:19.980 --> 00:15:22.670
Then I reveal my trap card!

00:15:22.670 --> 00:15:24.500
Regretful Rebirth.

00:15:24.500 --> 00:15:28.000
When a monster on my field 
is destroyed in battle,

00:15:28.000 --> 00:15:32.000
I can Special Summon that 
monster in defense position.

00:15:36.540 --> 00:15:39.590
Since I Special Summoned Shield Worm,

00:15:39.590 --> 00:15:43.590
to send another card in 
your deck to the graveyard.

00:15:43.770 --> 00:15:47.120
I'm sorry for acting on my own.

00:15:48.210 --> 00:15:51.800
Like I thought, his plan is…

00:15:55.360 --> 00:16:00.120
I summon Twin-Shield Defender in 
defense position and end my turn.

00:16:00.120 --> 00:16:01.640
Right.

00:16:06.000 --> 00:16:07.560
It's my turn.

00:16:08.230 --> 00:16:12.300
From my hand, I activate 
the spell card Worm Bait!

00:16:12.300 --> 00:16:15.260
When there's a monster 
on my field with "Worm"

00:16:15.260 --> 00:16:19.260
in its name, I can Special 
Summon two Worm Tokens.

00:16:22.450 --> 00:16:30.770
I release the two Worm Tokens to 
Advance Summon Dark Tuner Chaos Rogue!

00:16:33.400 --> 00:16:35.160
Dark Tuner?

00:16:35.480 --> 00:16:38.400
This is bad!  It's the same as before!

00:16:38.400 --> 00:16:39.360
What do you mean?

00:16:39.360 --> 00:16:40.100
It's…

00:16:40.100 --> 00:16:46.400
Level 8 Dark Tuner Chaos Rogue 
dark tunes Level 4 Shield Worm!

00:16:46.400 --> 00:16:47.970
Dark tuning?

00:16:54.170 --> 00:17:00.010
When shadow stacks on shadows, the 
door to the realm of the dead opens.

00:17:03.580 --> 00:17:05.890
A world without light!

00:17:06.980 --> 00:17:08.520
Dark Synchro!

00:17:08.520 --> 00:17:11.340
Come, Dark Diviner!

00:17:14.180 --> 00:17:17.370
What?  A Level negative 4 monster?

00:17:17.930 --> 00:17:20.430
That's right.  Light has turned into shadows!

00:17:20.910 --> 00:17:25.130
Dark Synchro allows me to summon a 
Synchro Monster whose Level is equal to

00:17:25.130 --> 00:17:30.130
the Level of one non-Tuner Monster 
subtracted by the Level of a Dark Tuner.

00:17:30.520 --> 00:17:36.010
That's right.  Yusei Fudo's opponent 
also did this unusual Synchro Summon.

00:17:36.010 --> 00:17:37.020
What?

00:17:37.700 --> 00:17:41.220
First, Dark Tuner Chaos Rogue's monster 
effect activates from the graveyard.

00:17:41.220 --> 00:17:47.920
When this card was used to Dark Synchro, five 
cards from your deck are sent to the graveyard.

00:17:48.480 --> 00:17:50.870
You're taking too much!

00:17:50.870 --> 00:17:57.170
Then my Dark Diviner attacks 
Strong Wind Dragon!

00:17:57.170 --> 00:18:02.200
I don't understand.  Strong Wind 
Dragon has higher attack points.

00:18:02.200 --> 00:18:04.290
He has a different goal!

00:18:04.670 --> 00:18:09.890
When Dark Diviner attacks, your monster's 
attack points become the same as Dark Diviner's.

00:18:09.890 --> 00:18:13.110
For every 100 points of change to its attack

00:18:13.110 --> 00:18:17.110
points, one card in your deck 
is sent to the graveyard.

00:18:17.770 --> 00:18:19.130
Deck destruction.

00:18:19.130 --> 00:18:24.170
That means 14 cards are sent to the 
graveyard!  How many cards are left?

00:18:24.170 --> 00:18:25.330
Nine cards.

00:18:26.530 --> 00:18:27.890
Nine?

00:18:30.640 --> 00:18:35.200
My goal is to take away 
your deck and your light.

00:18:35.200 --> 00:18:37.010
Dark Dragdown!

00:18:37.810 --> 00:18:39.170
It's mutual destruction!

00:18:42.700 --> 00:18:43.790
You!

00:18:45.470 --> 00:18:46.590
I'm fine.

00:18:46.590 --> 00:18:47.970
Hey!

00:18:48.740 --> 00:18:52.180
No matter how many times you attack, 
Strong Wind Dragon can't be

00:18:52.180 --> 00:18:56.180
destroyed in battle by a monster that 
has the same number of attack points!

00:18:56.530 --> 00:19:00.680
Dark Diviner also can't 
be destroyed in battle.

00:19:03.250 --> 00:19:07.400
I'm sorry.  This is all because 
I acted out on my own.

00:19:07.400 --> 00:19:11.150
I need at least this much 
entertainment to have fun.

00:19:11.730 --> 00:19:12.580
What's your name?

00:19:12.580 --> 00:19:14.230
It's Carly.

00:19:14.740 --> 00:19:17.100
Let's go, Carly.  This is the last draw!

00:19:19.530 --> 00:19:20.320
It's my and…

00:19:20.320 --> 00:19:22.180
And my…

00:19:22.180 --> 00:19:23.720
Turn!

00:19:25.850 --> 00:19:29.780
From my hand, I activate 
the spell card Mind Trust!

00:19:31.540 --> 00:19:35.100
By releasing one monster on 
my field, I can add a Tuner

00:19:35.100 --> 00:19:40.100
Monster in my graveyard with 
half its Level back to my hand.

00:19:41.530 --> 00:19:44.590
I release Level 6 Strong Wind Dragon!

00:19:44.590 --> 00:19:50.330
From my graveyard, I add the Level 3 
Tuner Monster Dark Resonator to my hand.

00:19:50.330 --> 00:19:52.330
I summon Dark Resonator!

00:19:55.860 --> 00:20:00.510
Then Dark Resonator tunes 
Twin-Shield Defender!

00:20:01.470 --> 00:20:03.150
The King's roar reverberates!

00:20:03.340 --> 00:20:06.580
The iron hammer of victory 
will destroy the land!

00:20:08.280 --> 00:20:09.790
Synchro Summon!

00:20:10.320 --> 00:20:13.710
Soar, Exploder Dragonwing!

00:20:14.180 --> 00:20:17.950
When this monster battles 
against a monster with fewer

00:20:17.950 --> 00:20:21.950
attack points, your monster is 
destroyed without damage calculation!

00:20:21.950 --> 00:20:27.080
Then you take damage equal to 
your monster's attack points!

00:20:27.080 --> 00:20:30.190
Incredible!  Back when you 
planned to activate Trust

00:20:30.190 --> 00:20:34.190
Mind, you already knew he was 
using a deck destruction strategy.

00:20:34.210 --> 00:20:35.700
No wonder you're the King.

00:20:36.190 --> 00:20:40.140
Exploder Dragonwing, attack Dark Diviner!

00:20:40.440 --> 00:20:42.120
King Storm!

00:21:09.060 --> 00:21:10.790
Where am I?

00:21:11.690 --> 00:21:16.260
It's the same as before.  It looks 
like someone was controlling him.

00:21:17.560 --> 00:21:18.490
Jack!

00:21:18.940 --> 00:21:22.020
Take me outside.

00:21:27.100 --> 00:21:32.540
At Jack Atlas's hospital, there was 
a flash of light and an explosion.

00:21:32.810 --> 00:21:37.610
What should I do?  What's 
going to happen now?

00:21:44.800 --> 00:21:45.890
Yusei.

00:21:45.890 --> 00:21:48.830
I'll tell you the truth.

00:21:49.700 --> 00:21:50.950
The truth?

00:22:13.470 --> 00:22:17.940
We look up and vow towards the shining light

00:22:18.300 --> 00:22:23.010
We will build our own future

00:22:23.480 --> 00:22:28.450
The far dawn shines blindingly

00:22:28.920 --> 00:22:33.630
Awaken in the wonderland

00:22:39.230 --> 00:22:48.770
The overflowing wave of emotions approaches

00:22:49.200 --> 00:22:54.340
This world can’t be solved using algorithms

00:22:54.410 --> 00:22:59.050
Even if it loses its light

00:22:59.510 --> 00:23:04.310
The hourglass behind the 
heart can’t be turned

00:23:04.320 --> 00:23:08.790
Roll the dice and get 
out and follow the light

00:23:08.990 --> 00:23:14.370
Fly towards tomorrow faster than a heartbeat

00:23:14.490 --> 00:23:19.230
This journey has no end

00:23:19.470 --> 00:23:24.710
There’s no meaning 
because there are no tears

00:23:25.140 --> 00:23:29.950
Hear my voice
